{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The פָּדֶר (peder)</b>. Onkelos translates it (Onkelos on Leviticus 1:8) as תַּרְבָּא, and so say all the commentators with one mouth. And the word has no cognate. In my opinion it is not a term for all the fats, but only for the thin fat that is spread out and separates between the entrails, and the word is from a metathesis: פֶּדֶר — פֶּרֶד, for it separates between the upper entrails and the lower ones. Therefore our Rabbis said (Yoma 26a) that one should spread the פֶּדֶר over the place of slaughter, for this is the way of honor above, since that fat is fit to spread and to cover with it. And so the dignitaries of the nations customarily spread it over the roast. And if it is a term for all the fats, it is called so on account of the fat that separates from the flesh, and so is its designation in the mouths of the natural philosophers, as I shall mention (Ramban on Leviticus 3:9):"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:49:24.046090708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}